<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shi Lang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1621–1696</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shi Lang was a Chinese admiral who served under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-zhilong">Zheng Zhilong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> before finally defecting to the Qing in 1651. In 1683 he destroyed the Zheng fleet at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Penghu</a>, leading to the surrender of the Kingdom of Tungning. He then persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a> to keep <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> as part of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shi-lang.jpg" alt="Shi Lang" width="282" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Generaal_Shi_Lang_met_een_gezelschap_hoogwaardigheidsbekleders_bij_een_waterput_aan_zee_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
